    "description": "<p>The purpose of this study is to determine the safety and effectiveness of genetically engineered CAR-T cells as a treatment for your dog's cancer. The CAR-T cells are made from your dog's own immune cells. Patients will be screened at the University of Pennsylvania's veterinary hospital to determine their eligibility for the study. This study will involve a screening visit for medical history and blood tests, a pre-conditioning visit, the treatment visit where the drug is administered, and monthly follow-up visits to assess the safety and effectiveness of the drug to treat your dog's cancer.</p>",
